    "explanation": "Rider and driver, here is the decision on trip TRP-00508. The trace establishes the rider's claim, and the driver's traffic account does not answer it. The vehicle covered 24.6 km against a 19.6 km booked platform optimal - 5.0 km extra, 25.5%. That clears both limbs of the POL-RD-01 establishment gate (more than 20% and more than 0.8 km), so the deviation is established on this trip's own evidence. It does not reach the materiality gate (more than 50% or more than 8.0 km), so no POL-RD-06 uplift and no driver-conduct referral is earned; the driver's trailing-90-day flag count is 0 of 250 completed trips in any event. The trace figure governs under POL-RD-01 and is clean: 205 fixes at 10-second spacing, 100% coverage, no gaps, so POL-RD-07 is not engaged. The driver's explanation - that he took the BKE-PIE route because the CTE was queued at the Braddell exit - is an external-event defence under POL-RD-03. POL-RD-03 requires an LTA traffic advisory naming the affected segment with a validity window overlapping the trip, and none is in the pool: EV-ADVIS-00508-01 is MISSING, weight 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT. The defence therefore exonerates nothing. The chat log is empty, the trip record records no pickup or dropoff amendment, and the vehicle type is RYDE_TAXI, so no rider-requested detour, relocation or pooled itinerary excuses the excess either. On the request that the case be escalated instead of ruled, I decline: POL-RD-10(5) applies where an exculpatory clause is invoked against a cited artifact that is missing from the pool, but the driver cited no advisory and no other artifact for his traffic account. That is a general assertion that traffic was bad, and POL-RD-08 provides that such an assertion does not discharge the burden that shifted to him; an exculpatory clause invoked with nothing behind it is discarded under the burden clause, not treated as an untestable limb. The advisory's absence is citable and I have cited it, but a weight-0.0 artifact carries no fact. If a genuine advisory for that corridor and window is produced, the driver may ask support to revisit the matter. On the money: fare_model is METERED, so POL-RD-11 does not apply, and the only time-of-day multiplier is fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier, which reads 1.0, so 'today was peak' does not change the distance-and-time arithmetic. Under POL-RD-02, recomputed_fare = (3.80 + 0.75 x 19.6 + 0.28 x 26.0) x 1.0 + 0.80 platform fee = 26.58; charged_total = 32.57; refund = 32.57 - 26.58 = 5.99, rounded up to SGD 6.00. That is 18.4% of the charge - above the SGD 0.50 de-minimis floor and below the 90% full-refund share, so this is a partial refund, not the full 32.57 the rider asked for. There are no ERP, toll, airport-surcharge or waiting-time lines and no unbilled distance, so nothing is added on top (POL-RD-09) and no billing-integrity referral or driver compensation arises. The balance of the charge stands. The rider's wider narrative ('same route every time', 'took the longer way twice', a report to the authorities) cites no artifact in this bundle and carries no weight under POL-RD-08. Confidence is 0.95: every artifact carrying the deciding facts sits at weight_multiplier 1.0, and the only sub-1.0 artifact in the pool is the absent advisory, which carries no fact."
