d fires. The case is decided rather than held.\n\nThe refund. fare_model is METERED, so POL-RD-02 governs and the refund is arithmetic. The surge multiplier is read from the fare breakdown, EV-FARE-00508, where it is 1.0. recomputed_fare = (3.80 + 0.75 × 19.6 + 0.28 × 26.0) × 1.0 + 0.80 = 26.58. charged_total is 32.57, so the refund is 32.57 − 26.58 = 5.99, rounded up to SGD 6.00. That is above the SGD 0.50 de minimis and 18.4% of the charge, well under the 90% share that would make it a full refund. There are no ERP gantry lines and no airport surcharge, so POL-RD-09 adds nothing, and off-route ERP could not have been added on top of the POL-RD-02 figure in any event.\n\nThe rider's wider narrative. 'Same route every time', 'took the longer way twice' and the reference to a usual fare under $40 cite no artifact; under POL-RD-08 they carry no weight, and the driver's 'today was peak' point does not touch the distance, because the only time-of-day multiplier on this fare is 1.0. The measure is the arithmetic above, not the whole SGD 32.57 that was asked for.\n\nOutcome: SGD 6.00 is returned to the rider; the balance of the charge stands; no driver compensation."
